      "quote": "Players can hit and defeat (essentially, kill) both passive and hostile creatures (also known as 'mobs'), as well as other players (if playing in multiplayer mode). There's also some use of weapons, such as swords, axes, bows, and TNT. However, the visual representation of the violence is limited by Minecraft's simple and cartoony style. There's no blood in any part of the game, neither coming from creatures nor the environment. Players can't die permanently and will respawn if their health reaches zero (unless they're playing on Hardcore mode, a sub-genre of Survival mode)."
